<DocsLayout
  title="Compose skills from durable primitives."
  description="Choose capability bundles, shared-state subgraphs, durable child runs, or guarded MCP Skills without creating a second execution engine."
  section="Skill composition"
>
  <aside
    class="docs-callout docs-callout--boundary"
    aria-labelledby="skill-composition-boundary-title"
  >
    <h2 id="skill-composition-boundary-title">
      A Skill is a bundle, not new authority
    </h2>
    <p>
      Compose versioned instructions, Tools, graphs, policies and configuration
      into one immutable Agent deployment. StateKnot deliberately keeps durable
      state, budgets, authorization and recovery on the existing audited paths.
      MCP Skill text and <code>allowed-tools</code> remain untrusted inputs.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="skill-composition-choice-title">
    <h2 id="skill-composition-choice-title">
      Choose the smallest durable boundary
    </h2>
    <div
      class="docs-table-wrap"
      tabindex="0"
      aria-label="Skill composition choices"
    >
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>Primitive</th><th>Boundary</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            ><td>Instructions plus independent Tools</td><td
              >Capability bundle</td
            ><td>No separate runtime state</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>Fixed multi-step shared-state flow</td><td
              >Shared-state subgraph</td
            ><td>One durable barrier per node</td></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>Isolated long-running work</td><td>Durable child run</td><td
              >Independent lifecycle and budget</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr
            ><td>Remote static package</td><td>MCP Skill activation</td><td
              >Verified untrusted content and guarded execution</td
            ></tr
          >
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      A Tool collection does not need a graph. Use a subgraph only when control
      flow itself must recover deterministically. Use a child run when state,
      ownership, deadline, budget or cancellation must be isolated.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="skill-composition-resolution-title">
    <h2 id="skill-composition-resolution-title">
      Resolve everything before admission
    </h2>
    <p>
      Pin exact module versions, reject cycles and collisions, topologically
      order dependencies and freeze one deployment snapshot. Prompt slots keep
      unique instruction identities, provenance and trust labels. Never merge
      remote Skill bytes into privileged system instructions. New configuration
      creates a new Agent version; old executables stay installed until their
      runs drain.
    </p>
    <p>
      Compile limits into existing Agent budgets, Tool execution limits, graph
      step bounds, child-run budgets and MCP acting windows. Conflicts choose
      the most restrictive compatible value or fail startup—composition never
      silently widens authority or resources.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="skill-composition-mcp-title">
    <h2 id="skill-composition-mcp-title">Keep MCP activation explicit</h2>
    <p>
      MCP catalog discovery never mutates an Agent. Each direct or nested remote
      Skill receives explicit policy approval, verified lazy reads, a durable
      acting window and per-operation permits. Execution still passes through
      the ordinary Tool registry and attempt ledger. Dynamic manifests,
      native-code hot loading and automatic discovery-to-Agent composition are
      not claimed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the <a
        href="https://github.com/StateKnot/StateKnot/blob/main/docs/skill-composition.md"
        >complete design and JiaClaw example</a
      >, then use <a href="/docs/mcp-skills/">MCP Skills</a> or
      <a href="/docs/graph-composition/">subgraphs and loops</a> for the selected
      boundary.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
